    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Who makes what",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about artists, books and films, and monuments.\n\n- **Names of artists:** many end in **-ista** and do not change: **el guitarrista**, **la guitarrista**, **el novelista**. Others end in **-or** and the feminine is **-ora**: **el escultor**, **la escultora**. Some are special: **el poeta**, **el bailarín** / **la bailarina**.\n- **Verbs:** crear, **diseñar** (to design), pintar un cuadro, componer música. You say «tener **imaginación**» and «ser un **genio**».\n- **Books:** a detective or historical novel, a **biografía** (the life of someone).\n- **Films:** a **comedia**, a drama, a horror film, an action film.\n- **Monuments:** a **palacio**, an **acueducto**, the **muralla** that surrounds the **casco antiguo**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Masculine and feminine of artists",
     "texto": [
      "Names for people follow several patterns:\n\n- **-ista** does not change: **el / la guitarrista**, **el / la pianista**, **el / la novelista**, **el / la artista**.\n- **-or** → **-ora**: **el escultor / la escultora**, **el diseñador / la diseñadora**, **el traductor / la traductora**.\n- **-ín** → **-ina**: **el bailarín / la bailarina**.\n- **-ante** does not change either: **el / la cantante**.\n- Special cases: **el poeta**, and for a woman **la poeta** or **la poetisa**.\n\nThe practical rule: look at the last syllable and remember the pattern."
     ],
